cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "Additive Structure of Phonological Correspondences: A protoform-agnostic method for discovering mathematical patterns in documented linguistic systems"
abstract: >-
  A reconstruction-free method that represents each attested sound correspondence
  as the set of phonological features that differ between two aligned segments (a
  symmetric operator), turning a language family into a measurable repertoire of
  feature-difference vectors, and studies its geometry and additive structure
  against explicit null models — with the historical apparatus kept out of the
  computation so it can serve as an independent test.
